  {
    "name": "update-explicit-clear: an explicit empty due_on goes on the wire as \"\", with no GET",
    "description": "BC3's JSON card update is presence-aware since basecamp/bc3#12521: an omitted key is left unchanged and an explicit \"\" clears (Rails blank-cast, pinned by a BC3 server test). So a clear MUST put the key on the wire as the empty string. Omission no longer clears — it means \"leave unchanged\", which is exactly how released SDKs (<= v0.12.0) silently no-op against production. A literal null is not an option either: it would violate body compaction (SPEC section 18) and five of the six SDKs strip nulls before the wire, whereas none of them strip \"\". This case is the cross-SDK pin for that encoding.",
    "operation": "UpdateCard",
    "method": "PUT",
    "path": "/card_tables/cards/{cardId}",
    "pathParams": {
      "cardId": 1069479350
    },
    "requestBody": {
      "due_on": ""
    },
    "mockResponses": [
